<%# Animation picker modal — opened from the "Change animation" CTA on a card's
    left panel. The animation counterpart of the media picker.

    TWO panes, one modal, because two card types have an animation and they are
    different things: a Range card picks a reaction CHARACTER (a looping Lottie
    per set), an NPS card picks the liquid CONTAINER it fills. The creator's
    action is the same in both cases — "change this card's animation" — so
    splitting it into two modals would be two names for one job. Which pane
    opens is decided by the CTA (animation-picker#open vs #openShapes).

    Either pick drives the card's own hidden <select>, so survey-editor does the
    live swap + autosave and the visual picker shares ONE apply path with any
    keyboard/SR use. %>
<div class="media-modal-backdrop"
     data-animation-picker-target="backdrop"
     data-action="click->animation-picker#backdropClick"
     hidden>
  <div class="media-modal anim-modal" data-animation-picker-target="modal">

    <div class="media-modal-head">
      <div class="media-modal-title"><%= t("editor.animation_modal_title", default: "Choose an animation") %></div>
      <button type="button" class="media-modal-close"
              data-action="click->animation-picker#close"
              aria-label="<%= t("editor.close", default: "Close") %>">✕</button>
    </div>

    <div class="media-modal-body">

      <%# ── Range: the reaction character ── %>
      <div data-animation-picker-target="lottiePane">
        <p class="anim-modal-sub"><%= t("editor.animation_modal_sub", default: "This character reacts as respondents drag the slider. It's picked to match your Verto's theme — swap it any time.") %></p>

        <% range_theme_groups.each do |category, opts| %>
          <div class="anim-group">
            <div class="anim-group-label"><%= category %></div>
            <div class="anim-grid">
              <% opts.each do |label, slug| %>
                <button type="button" class="anim-option"
                        role="option" aria-selected="false"
                        data-slug="<%= slug %>"
                        data-animation-picker-target="option"
                        data-action="click->animation-picker#pick"
                        title="<%= label %>">
                  <span class="anim-option-preview"
                        data-animation-picker-target="preview"
                        data-slug="<%= slug %>"></span>
                  <span class="anim-option-label"><%= label %></span>
                </button>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <%# ── NPS: the liquid container ──
          The tiles are the real vessel SVG, part-filled, rather than a picture
          of one: an NPS container has no still frame to preview the way a
          Lottie set does, and an empty silhouette doesn't read as something
          that fills up. Server-rendered because the drawing is already a
          server-side helper — no second code path, and no Lottie to mount. %>
      <div data-animation-picker-target="shapePane" hidden>
        <p class="anim-modal-sub"><%= t("editor.nps_animation_modal_sub", default: "Respondents drag to fill this container to their answer. It's picked to match your Verto's theme — swap it any time.") %></p>

        <% nps_shape_groups.each do |category, opts| %>
          <div class="anim-group">
            <div class="anim-group-label"><%= category %></div>
            <div class="anim-grid">
              <% opts.each do |label, slug| %>
                <button type="button" class="anim-option anim-option-shape"
                        role="option" aria-selected="false"
                        data-slug="<%= slug %>"
                        data-animation-picker-target="shapeOption"
                        data-action="click->animation-picker#pickShape"
                        title="<%= label %>">
                  <span class="anim-option-preview"><%= nps_shape_preview(slug) %></span>
                  <span class="anim-option-label"><%= label %></span>
                </button>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</div>
